my name is Karolina Aisha I am a  mathematician working at the Institute  for pure and applied mathematics in Rio  de Janeiro Brazil so I work mostly with  the mathematical research and I also  teach graduate classes here I think  so there is a sort of collective of  women in mathematics in Brazil that  evolved organically over the last few  years and culminated with the  organization of the world meeting for  women in mathematics in 2018 so in  preparation for that we organized a  series of roundtables about women in  mathematics throughout the country and  this had a global coordination but local  organizers in each University and that  was very empowering not only strengthen  the the local groups of women in  mathematics but also connected them into  a bigger Network and now we are  preparing for 2019 the first Brazilian  meeting for women in mathematics will  happen in July  so whenever I am involved in some  projects working with other people with  other with groups of people I tried to  work as horizontal as possible  and listening to try to make the  decision move collective as opposed to  too hierarchical and this is because I  really believe that when there is a  group working together a new  intelligence emerges and it's a group  intelligence that is only possible if  one works horizontally
 

